<title>FRANCE: Algeria launches 150,000-tonne durum tender.</title>
<headline>Algeria launches 150,000-tonne durum tender.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Algeria on Monday launched a snap tender to import 150,000 tonnes of durum wheat between mid-March and the end of April, European grain traders said.</p>
<p>Traders must submit offers on Monday for a reply on Thursday, they said.</p>
<p>The tender calls for shipments of 50,000 tonnes each over three periods -- March 16-31, April 1-15 and April 16-30.</p>
<p>Algeria says it will consider durum from the United States, Canada or Syria, the traders said.</p>
</text>
